# Creative UI & Taste Rules

Use these rules whenever you change layout, styling, or visual components. Keep text at WCAG AA contrast. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not restyle a working flow into a fake screen.

## 1. Anti-generic layout

- Never build a standard "image on the left, text on the right" band.
- Use asymmetric grids, bento groupings, and editorial whitespace.
- Overlap sections with negative margins, absolute anchors, and a clear z-index. The overlap must not cover a control.

```css
/* ❌ centered card on a flat gray page */
.panel { margin: 0 auto; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #ddd; }

/* ✅ type and surface share one composition */
.stage { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 0.8fr; }
.surface { margin-left: -40px; z-index: 2; }
```

## 2. Visual polish

- Typography leads. Pair a large tight headline with small quiet meta text.
- No generic diagonal gradients. Use soft radial orbs, a mesh of radial stops, or a strict monochrome palette with a thin accent stroke.
- Glass, not hard cards: `backdrop-filter`, a 1px translucent border, and a layered shadow.

```css
.glass {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
  backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8), 0 24px 50px rgba(26, 29, 33, 0.1);
}
```

## 3. Motion

- Every button, card, and link has a transition. Use `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` over about 0.5s.
- Reveal layout with CSS keyframes or Framer Motion: a short rise and fade, staggered. No bounce.
- Do not animate `outline`. Do not use `transition: all`.

```css
.btn { transition: transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), box-shadow 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
.btn:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .btn { transition: none; }
}
```
